# Only what the Dockerfile copies is sent to the build: the package
# metadata, the lockfile, the files the package's own README metadata
# reads, and `src/`. Everything else stays out so a stray local file
# (a virtual environment, a scan's evidence, a test fixture) can never
# land in the image.
*
!pyproject.toml
!uv.lock
!README.md
!CHANGELOG.md
!LICENSE
!NOTICE
!src/
src/**/__pycache__/
